{"tool_name":"light-seq","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"light-seq","home":"http://lightseq.io","license":"MIT","summary":"Light-directed in situ barcoding of biomolecules in fixed cells and tissues for spatially indexed sequencing.","addition_date":"2022-12-27T15:46:30.020520Z","last_update_date":"2022-12-27T15:46:30.023046Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:light-seq","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"cepko@genetics.med.harvard.edu","name":"Constance L. Cepko","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9945-6387","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"jocelyn.y.kishi@gmail.com","name":"Jocelyn Y. Kishi","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4352-1159","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"py@hms.harvard.edu","name":"Peng Yin","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2769-6357","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"sinem.saka@embl.de","name":"Sinem K. Saka","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5017-379X","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"DNA barcoding","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3200"},{"term":"Gene expression profiling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0314"},{"term":"Microscope image visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3552"},{"term":"Parsing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_1812"}]}],"name":"Light-Seq","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/S41592-022-01604-1","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2022, The Author(s).We present Light-Seq, an approach for multiplexed spatial indexing of intact biological samples using light-directed DNA barcoding in fixed cells and tissues followed by ex situ sequencing. Light-Seq combines spatially targeted, rapid photocrosslinking of DNA barcodes onto complementary DNAs in situ with a one-step DNA stitching reaction to create pooled, spatially indexed sequencing libraries. This light-directed barcoding enables in situ selection of multiple cell populations in intact fixed tissue samples for full-transcriptome sequencing based on location, morphology or protein stains, without cellular dissociation. Applying Light-Seq to mouse retinal sections, we recovered thousands of differentially enriched transcripts from three cellular layers and discovered biomarkers for a very rare neuronal subtype, dopaminergic amacrine cells, from only four to eight individual cells per section. Light-Seq provides an accessible workflow to combine in situ imaging and protein staining with next generation sequencing of the same cells, leaving the sample intact for further analysis post-sequencing.","authors":[{"name":"Cepko C.L."},{"name":"Jordanides J.J."},{"name":"Kishi J.Y."},{"name":"Liu N."},{"name":"Saka S.K."},{"name":"Serrata M."},{"name":"Sheng K."},{"name":"West E.R."},{"name":"Yin P."}],"date":"2022-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"Light-Seq: light-directed in situ barcoding of biomolecules in fixed cells and tissues for spatially indexed sequencing"},"pmcid":"PMC9636025","pmid":"36216958"},{"doi":"10.1038/S41592-022-01608-X","metadata":{"date":"2022-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"Light-Seq: from microscopy to transcriptomics and back"},"pmid":"36253646"}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene transcripts","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3512"},{"term":"Imaging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3382"},{"term":"Mapping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0102"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"},{"term":"Transcriptomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3308"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Light-Seq","home":"https://bio.tools/light-seq","license":"MIT","summary":"Light-directed in situ barcoding of biomolecules in fixed cells and tissues for spatially indexed sequencing.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metri